From: mscharged-port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Diagnostic switches for platform lighting differences
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host diagnostics, off by default. Apply after 0076.

The macOS/Metal build renders lit 3D scenes about half as bright as Linux and
Dolphin. Two environment switches help locate the cause on a machine without
a debugger: AURORA_DEBUG_LIGHT_LOG=1 prints every distinct light, lighting
channel and TEV colour setting once (to diff platforms), and
AURORA_DEBUG_NO_DUAL_SOURCE=1 leaves dual-source blending off so the alpha
pre-pass fallback runs. Neither changes anything when unset.

